{
  "slug": "aws-agents",
  "name": "Aws Agents",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Build, deploy, and operate AI agents on AWS. Skills for scaffolding agents with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, connecting tools, memory, policies, evaluation, debugging, and production hardening.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `agents-build` (Use to extend an existing agent project with memory, app integration, VPC, multi-agent, migration, model, browser, code interpreter,…), `agents-connect` (Use when connecting your agent to external APIs, tools, or services via Gateway, or restricting tool access with…), `agents-debug` (Use when your agent or environment is broken — wrong answers, errors, timeouts, tool failures, or CLI issues), `agents-deploy` (Use when deploying your agent to AWS, or when a deploy has failed), `agents-get-started` (Use when a developer wants to create a new agent project or get started with AgentCore), `agents-harden` (Use when preparing your agent for production — IAM scoping, inbound auth (JWT, SigV4), secrets management, cold start…), `agents-optimize` (Use when measuring or improving agent quality and performance — set up evaluators, online monitoring, CI/CD quality gates,…), `agents-pay` (Use when THIS agent needs to pay for x402-protected content at runtime: hitting a paywall mid-task, settling it…)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `awsknowledge`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install aws-agents@claude-plugins-official` from `aws/agent-toolkit-for-aws` (`plugins/aws-agents`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 8,
    "mcp": 1
  },
